ild's head (class `returned`, provenance tenant, no adapter run — the shape `attavo verify` already writes for a forge that is not green), so the rejection is a record and not a level; the next build attempt is handed the evidence; counsel is asked only when the second attempt ends with the same signature. Every other non-pass record is read by counsel as today, and counsel's verdict routes: `answer` starts the next attempt with the answer as its steer; `patch` files and the report reads \\\"waiting on #N\\\"; `person` is the operator's. A question, a claims-boundary stop, a tenant's gate refusal, and an environment refusal are never retried by this item; environment refusal is recorded here and acted on by R4's breaker.\\n\\nOne budget. `[drive].attempts` (default 3) per stage, shared by plain, returned, and steered attempts; every attempt with a marker counts, a recovered one included, because the budget bounds what the product spends on a stage. Two attempts of one stage ending with the identical failure signature stop the stage early and do not spend the third. When the budget is spent, or the early stop fires, the report's state is `stopped` and it carries `attempts`: for each attempt its class, signature, the bound it crossed (`stall`, `ceiling`, or none), wall clock and cost; whether the signatures match; and `rulings_available` naming what each would do (`--again` resets the budget, flagged unlikely to help when the signatures match; amending the spec, which moves the approval). Counsel is read once more at exhaustion and its sentence rides beside the comparison, never instead of it.\\n\\nThe signature. Every non-pass stop carries `stop.signature`, a string a script computes from the record and compares by equality, with runs of digits removed: for `died` and `hung`, the last event line; for `transient`, the adapter's stop detail; for a `returned` check rejection, the sorted names of the required checks that concluded red; for a `returned` review, the sorted