ure, the schema keys, the doctor's refusal, a pass that retries the four families inside the budget with the early stop and the transient wait, the returned record on a red check with its log handed to the next build, and the ceiling. It has no steer, no blocking-finding return, no transient wait in the report's words, no `--again` narrowing, no adapter classification, and no updates to the existing tests the stop shape and the doctor's refusal break. Ten of the eleven tests in `tests/test_retry.py` are red on the tree; five are red on the stub, listed in the issue. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the built tree with no `type: ignore`.\\n\\nRetires: the operator as the only thing that runs a stage a second time; `blocked-on-checks` as a level with no record behind it (with it, `tests/test_drive.py::test_drive_pass_reads_a_red_forge_as_blocked_and_starts_nothing` and `test_drive_until_ready_stops_when_the_forge_goes_red_after_a_build`, which encode that level, are rewritten to the returned record); the counsel run on a vendor's capacity error (#194's `verify-01`, replayed as this item's rejection fixture); the stall bound as a bound on adapters that do not stream; `--again` inside the budget.\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- attavo/drive.py\\n- attavo/report.py\\n- attavo/verify.py\\n- attavo/build.py\\n- attavo/stops.py\\n- attavo/doctor.py\\n- attavo/types.py\\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\\n- schema/records/build.schema.json\\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\\n- schema/drive-report.schema.json\\n- adapters/fixture/run\\n- adapters/fixture/conformance.json\\n- adapters/claude-code/run\\n- adapters/claude-code/conformance.json\\n- adapters/codex/run\\n- adapters/codex/conformance.json\\n- attavo.toml\\n- tests/test_retry.py\\n- tests/test_pass.py\\n- tests/test_drive.py\\n- tests/test_report.py\\n- tests/test_doctor.py\\n- tests/test_build.py\\n- tests/test_verify.py\\n- tests/test_verify_polls.py\\n- tests/test_proof_five_elsewhere.py\\n- tests/test_record_schemas.py\\n- tests/test_stub_ratio.py\\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- a-transient-stop-retries-plainly.sh: on a fixture tenant whose build adapter refuses once with the vendor's capacity error and passes on its second run, passes alone carry the item from an approved spec to a passing build-02 whose retry_of is build-01, build-01's stop class is transient, and no counsel record exists\\n- a-red-check-becomes-a-returned-record-and-the-next-build-is-handed-its-log.sh: on a fixture tenant whose checks command reads red once after the first build and green after, a pass writes verify-01 with status returned and class returned naming the red check in its signature, the next pass starts build-02 whose first feedback file names that check and its log, and no operator act occurs between approval and the passing review\\n- two-identical-failures-stop-at-two-and-the-report-compares-them.sh: on a fixture tenant whose build adapter dies on the same event line every run, passes write build-01 and build-02 as died with equal signatures and start no build-03; attavo drive N --report reads stopped with two attempts, matching signatures, and --again among the rulings available\\n- a-stage-past-its-ceiling-is-hung-by-the-ceiling.sh: on a fixture tenant whose build adapter sleeps past a ceiling of two seconds and declares it does not stream, a pass terminates the worker and writes build-01 as hung with bound ceiling, and the report never speaks of event age\\n- the-manifest-and-the-tests-exist.sh: the doctor refuses a fixture manifest with a [drive] table and no ceilings, and tests/test_retry.py carries the tests named\\n\",\"numLines\":65,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":65}}}\n+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CfRLtQy1BEnDFXxqdehTe\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01Q6Ube5ZXktvyXamyPZVUc8\",\"name\":\"Edit\",\"input\":{\"replace_all\":false,\"file_path\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-219/attavo/build.py\",\"old_string\":\"BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET = 3\\n\\nBUILD_HALT_EXIT = 3\\n\\nCHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES = 200\",\"new_string\":\"BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET = 3\\n\\nBUILD_HALT_EXIT = 3\\n\\nCHECKS_FEEDBACK_TAIL_LINES = 200\\n\\n\\ndef _steer_seed(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], prior_stem: str) -> tuple[str | None, str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"(steer_stem, text): the counsel record that read prior_stem, when its\\n    verdict is \\\"answer\\\" -- R3's own steer, the newest ruling newer than the\\n    blocking record itself (an operator's ruling, after R4, is the other\\n    kind; this item carries only counsel's). (\\\"\\\", None) when no such\\n    counsel record exists, or it did not answer.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from attavo.counsel import counsel_record_for\\n    item_records_dir = prior_stem  # placeholder, unused; real call passes records_dir\\n    raise NotImplementedError\\n\\n\\ndef _retry_seed(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], records_dir: Path\\n                ) -> tuple[str | None, str | None, str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"(retry_of, steer, feedback): what a retried build's first iteration\\n    is handed (R3) -- the prior attempt's own class and signature, the\\n    evidence a returned review carries (a red required check's log, read\\n    through [forge].check_log_command, or a review's own blocking\\n    findings), and the newest steer newer than the blocking record\\n    (counsel's answer text, named by the record it came from). A build\\n    retries the latest build record that is not a pass, or the latest\\n    verify record that returned it (class returned, its own build_sha\\n    matching the latest build's) -- one or the other, never both: a\\n    returned review is read only once its own build has already passed,\\n    so a not-pass build record and a returned verify record naming that\\n    same build never coexist. (\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\") on a first attempt -- nothing\\n    to retry, nothing to seed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from attavo.stops import counsel_record_for\\n    latest_build = cast(\\\"dict[str, Any] | None\\\", latest_record(records_dir, \\\"build\\\"))\\n    latest_verify = cast(\\\"dict[str, Any] | None\\\", latest_record(records_dir, \\\"verify\\\"))\\n    prior_stem = f\\\"build-{next_attempt_number(records_dir, 'build') - 1:02d}\\\"\\n    prior: dict[str, Any] | None = None\\n    prior_verify_stem: str | None = None\\n    if (latest_verify and (latest_verify.get(\\\"stop\\\") or {}).get(\\\"class\\\") == \\\"returned\\\"\\n            and latest_build and latest_verify.get(\\\"build_sha\\\") == latest_build.get(\\\"sha\\\")):\\n        prior = latest_verify\\n        verify_attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, \\\"verify\\\")\\n        prior_verify_stem = f\\\"verify-{max(verify_attempts):02d}\\\" if verify_attempts else None\\n    elif latest_build and latest_build.get(\\\"status\\\") != \\\"pass\\\":\\n        prior = latest_build\\n    if prior is None:\\n        return None, None, \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    stop: dict[str, Any] = prior.get(\\\"stop\\\") or {}\\n    lines = [f\\\"attempt {prior_verify_stem or prior_stem} stopped as {stop.get('class')}: \\\"\\n            f\\\"{stop.get('detail') or ''}\\\",\\n            f\\\"signature: {stop.get('signature') or ''}\\\", \\\"\\\"]\\n\\n    forge = m.get(\\\"forge\\\") or {}\\n    if stop.get(\\\"class\\\") == \\\"returned\\\":\\n        findings = prior.get(\\\"findings\\\")\\n        if findings:\\n            lines.append(\\\"blocking findings:\\\")\\n            for finding in findings:\\n                if str(finding.get(\\\"severity\\\")) != \\\"blocking\\\":\\n                    continue\\n                lines.append(f\\\"- {finding.get('title')}: {finding.get('specimen')} \\\"\\n                             f\\\"(retires: {finding.get('retires')})\\\")\\n            lines.append(\\\"\\\")\\n        elif forge.get(\\\"check_log_command\\\"):\\n            for c in (prior.get(\\\"forge_checks\\\") or {}).get(\\\"conclusions\\\") or []:\\n                if c.get(\\\"conclusion\\\") in (\\\"success\\\", \\\"neutral\\\", \\\"skipped\\\"):\\n                    continue\\n                run = subprocess.run(\\n                    f\\\"{forge['check_log_command']} {shlex.quote(str(prior.get('sha')))} \\\"\\n                    f\\\"{shlex.quote(c['name'])}\\\", shell=True, cwd=str(root),\\n                    capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n                lines += [f\\\"--- check {c['name']} {c['conclusion']} ---\\\",\\n                         run.stdout.strip(), \\\"\\\"]\\n\\n    steer_stem: str | None = None\\n    counsel = counsel_record_for(records_dir, \\\"build\\\" if prior_verify_stem is None else \\\"verify\\\",\\n                                 int((prior_verify_stem or prior_stem).rsplit(\\\"-\\\", 1)[1]))\\n    if counsel is not None and counsel.get(\\\"verdict\\\") == \\\"answer\\\":\\n        counsel_attempts = parse_attempts(records_dir, \\\"counsel\\\")\\n        nn = max((n for n, rec in counsel_attempts.items() if rec is counsel), default=None)\\n        if nn is not None:\\n            steer_stem = f\\\"counsel-{nn:02d}\\\"\\n            answer = (counsel.get(\\\"proposal\\\") or {}).get(\\\"ruling_text\\\")\\n            if answer:\\n                lines += [f\\\"steer from {steer_stem}:\\\", answer.strip(), \\\"\\\"]\\n\\n    retry_of = prior_verify_stem if prior_verify_stem is not None else prior_stem\\n    return retry_of, steer_stem, \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines) + \\\"\\\\n\\\"\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2130,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":319234,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2130},\"output_tokens\":15,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":nul