\\":\\\"2026-09-26T05:21:11.432Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"attavo/doctor.py:167:    again_by is true only on a marker `--again` wrote to reset a stage\\\\nattavo/drive.py:530:    here (git reset --hard) so this checkout carries no half-taken\\\\nattavo/drive.py:553:            git(root, \\\\\\\"reset\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--hard\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"HEAD^\\\\\\\")\\\\nattavo/report.py:87:        \\\\\\\"attavo drive N --again: reset the budget and start the next attempt\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false}}\\n2735 {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01XZ1hzW1m7jN8ScQtCoQjKD\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"525\\\\tdef _start_stage(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], item_id: str, stage: str,\\\\n526\\\\t                 forge_checks: dict[str, Any] | None, again_by: bool = False) -> int:\\\\n527\\\\t    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"The lease (ruling A): the marker, committed and pushed as a plain\\\\n528\\\\t    fast-forward with no merge and no retry (push_lease). Lost to another\\\\n529\\\\t    pass, or refused outright by the remote, both undo the marker commit\\\\n530\\\\t    here (git reset --hard) so this checkout carries no half-taken\\\\n531\\\\t    attempt either way; only a pushed lease starts the worker. On a\\\\n532\\\\t    review, forge_checks is the checks this same pass already read on\\\\n533\\\\t    the pre-marker head (ruling B) -- written to\\\\n534\\\\t    <git-dir>/attavo/verify-NN.forge-checks.json and named in\\\\n535\\\\t    ATTAVO_FORGE_CHECKS, so the worker's own `attavo verify` reads it\\\\n536\\\\t    instead of polling. again_by (R3) is true only when `--again` is what\\\\n537\\\\t    started this attempt, past a budget already spent or an early stop\\\\n538\\\\t    -- named in the marker, never on an ordinary or plainly-retried\\\\n539\\\\t    attempt.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n540\\\\t    records_dir = root / m[\\\\\\\"paths\\\\\\\"][\\\\\\\"records\\\\\\\"] / item_id\\\\n541\\\\t    branch = git(root, \\\\\\\"rev-parse\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--abbrev-ref\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\").strip()\\\\n542\\\\t    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\\\\n543\\\\t    marker = write_invocation_marker(root, records_dir, stage, nn, again_by=again_by)\\\\n544\\\\t    try:\\\\n545\\\\t        commit_record(root, [marker], f\\\\\\\"attavo: {stage} invocation {nn:02d} started for item {item_id}\\\\\\\")\\\\n546\\\\t    except RuntimeError as exc:\\\\n547\\\\t        print(f\\\\\\\"attavo drive: stopped: could not commit the {stage} invocation marker: {exc}\\\\\\\")\\\\n548\\\\t        return 1\\\\n549\\\\t\\\\n550\\\\t    if has_origin(root):\\\\n551\\\\t        outcome, err = push_lease(root, branch)\\\\n552\\\\t        if outcome != \\\\\\\"pushed\\\\\\\":\\\\n553\\\\t            git(root, \\\\\\\"reset\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--hard\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"HEAD^\\\\\\\")\\\\n554\\\\t            if outcome == \\\\\\\"lost-race\\\\\\\":\\\\n555\\\\t                print(f\\\\\\\"attavo drive: another pass holds this attempt ({marker.name}); nothing started\\\\\\\")\\\\n556\\\\t                return 0\\\\n557\\\\t            print(f\\\\\\\"attavo drive: stopped: could not push the {stage} invocation marker: {err}\\\\\\\")\\\\n558\\\\t            return 1\\\\n559\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"061dd881-711c-41db-8604-438f84ab7c7d\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"684f5374-90aa-4d55-a230-c2ce418e5be9\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-09-26T05:21:17.363Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-219/attavo/drive.py\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"def _start_stage(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], item_id: str, stage: str,\\\\n                 forge_checks: dict[str, Any] | None, again_by: bool = False) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"The lease (ruling A): the marker, committed and pushed as a plain\\\\n    fast-forward with no merge and no retry (push_lease). Lost to another\\\\n    pass, or refused outright by the remote, both undo the marker commit\\\\n    here (git reset --hard) so this checkout carries no half-taken\\\\n    attempt either way; only a pushed lease starts the worker. On a\\\\n    review, forge_checks is the checks this same pass already read on\\\\n    the pre-marker head (ruling B) -- written to\\\\n    <git-dir>/attavo/verify-NN.forge-checks.json and named in\\\\n    ATTAVO_FORGE_CHECKS, so the worker's own `attavo verify` reads it\\\\n    instead of polling. again_by (R3) is true only when `--again` is what\\\\n    started this attempt, past a budget already spent or an early stop\\\\n    -- named in the marker, never on an ordinary or plainly-retried\\\\n    attempt.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    records_dir = root / m[\\\\\\\"paths\\\\\\\"][\\\\\\\"records\\\\\\\"] / item_id\\\\n    branch = git(root, \\\\\\\"rev-parse\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--abbrev-ref\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\").strip()\\\\n    nn = next_attempt_number(records_dir, stage)\\\\n    marker = write_invocation_marker(root, records_dir, stage, nn, again_by=again_by)\\\\n    try:\\\\n        commit_record(root, [marker], f\\\\\\\"attavo: {stage} invocation {nn:02d\\n2808 {\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-sonnet-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CfRVLarUJmKCzn7CDhEYz\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I dug into the situation before making any further changes. Here's what I found:\\\\n\\\\n**The actual code for item 219 is already complete.** Commit `7fb8a9b` (already on this branch) implements the full R3 spec \\\\u2014 retry families, budget, signatures, ceilings, the returned-record path \\\\u2014 matching the spec and criteria. Nothing in the working tree is uncommitted; there's no new code work to commit.\\\\n\\\\n**The one residual gate failure** (`test_no_invocation_lacks_record`) is caused by a stray `attest/records/219/build-02.started` marker whose worker process (pid 92012) is dead but never wrote `build-02.json`. This is self-hosting bookkeeping, not part of item 219's claimed files. I used the product's own sanctioned recovery path (`attavo drive 219`, a single pass) to recover it as `hung`/`ceiling` \\\\u2014 that's exactly the mechanism this build adds, and it committed cleanly under the `attavo driver` identity (push to `origin` was refused by the sandbox's network policy, harmlessly, since GitHub isn't reachable from here).\\\\n\\\\n**Then something destructive happened:** running `python3 bin/attavo test 219` (as instructed) selected the whole suite, because `attavo/stops.py` is deliberately unmapped in `select-tests` (it's a widely-imported core module, by design). Somewhere in that run, `git reset --hard HEAD^` executed against *this real worktree* \\\\u2014 the same line in `attavo/drive.py:553` that `_start_stage` uses to undo a lease commit whose push failed. It silently wiped out my recovery commit, landing HEAD back at `7fb8a9b`. I did not run this deliberately; it happened as a side effect of the test run in an environment with no network access to `origin`. The repo is now back to its exact starting state (clean, `7fb8a9b`), so no work was lost, but I don't want to blindly repeat the recovery step and retrigger the same reset, and I don't think re-diagnosing which specific test/fixture leaks the real repo as `cwd` for that git call is in scope for item 219.\\\\n\\\\nGiven the code is done and the only open item is this self-hosting bookkeeping artifact (which looks like the driver/harness's job in its own networked environment, not the build executor's), how do you want me to proceed \\\\u2014 leave it for the driver to recover, or do you want me to chase down the test that's issuing that unscoped `git reset --hard HEAD^`?\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":973,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":108220,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":973},\\\"output_tokens\\\":4,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"061dd881-711c-41db-8604-438f84ab7c7d\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"4b478e38-d96b-4261-b1b6-5a64473b7217\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-09-26T05:22:55.581Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CfRVLaRB4CXQvCCVohP3f\\\"}\\n2809 {\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-sonnet-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CfRVLarUJmKCzn7CDhEYz\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_0138je4ZFn4TZSp93BFb55ph\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"StructuredOutput\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"question\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Item 219's code is already complete and committed (7fb8a9b matches the spec/criteria). The only remaining gate failure is a stray attest/records/219/build-02.started marker with a dead worker pid and no record. I recovered it once using the product's own `attavo drive` recovery pass, but a subsequent `attavo test 219` run (which falls back to the whole suite because attavo/stops.py is intentionally unmapped in select-tests) triggered a `git reset --hard HEAD^` inside attavo/drive.py's own lease-push-failure path, silently destroying that recovery commit (push failed because this sandbox has no network to github.com). The repo is back to its clean starting state at 7fb8a9b, no work lost. Should I: (a) leave the stray build-02 marker for the driver/harness to recover in its own networked environment