{"findings": [{"title": "Ceiling recovery targets the pass PID, not the over-ceiling worker", "specimen": "attavo/doctor.py::write_invocation_marker records os.getpid() before attavo/drive.py::_start_stage spawns the detached worker; attavo/drive.py::_recover_one later sends SIGTERM to that marker PID. The worker can therefore survive a ceiling recovery and subsequently write a competing record.", "retires": "The claim that stage ceilings terminate workers, rather than merely recording them as hung while their work continues.", "rejection_test": "tests/test_retry.py::test_ceiling_recovery_terminates_the_actual_worker_and_it_cannot_write_a_late_record", "severity": "Harmless only when the worker has already exited independently; blocking when an alive worker crosses its ceiling and continues running after recovery."}, {"title": "Recovered retry attempts lose retry_of and steer provenance", "specimen": "attavo/drive.py::_recover_one unconditionally writes \"retry_of\": null and \"steer\": null, including for build-02/verify-02 markers started as retries. This contradicts the required record shape for every retried attempt.", "retires": "Ambiguous recovered records that cannot identify the prior attempt or the counsel steer whose input they consumed.", "rejection_test": "tests/test_retry.py::test_a_recovered_retried_attempt_records_retry_of_and_steer", "severity": "Harmless for a first attempt; blocking when attempt 02 or later dies or hangs and its recovered record omits its retry lineage."}, {"title": "Exhaustion caused by recovery never receives the required final counsel read", "specimen": "attavo/drive.py::_stage_body invokes counsel after an ordinarily completed non-pass record exhausts the budget, but attavo/drive.py::_recover_one commits died/hung records directly and never invokes counsel. Two identical recovered failures therefore stop early without the exhaustion sentence required beside the comparison.", "retires": "Exhaustion reports that present only mechanical attempt comparison and omit counsel\u2019s final interpretation.", "rejection_test": "tests/test_retry.py::test_two_identical_recovered_failures_run_counsel_once_at_exhaustion_and_report_its_sentence", "severity": "Harmless while recovery leaves retry budget available; blocking when a recovered died or hung record spends the budget or triggers the identical-signature early stop."}, {"title": "Questions are retried after counsel answer despite being explicitly non-retryable", "specimen": "attavo/drive.py::NEVER_RETRIED_CLASSES omits question, and retry_state consequently starts another attempt when counsel answers one. tests/test_retry.py::test_counsels_verdict_routes_the_next_pass positively encodes this divergence even though the approved spec and build commit both say a question is never retried by this item.", "retires": "Automatic reruns after a stop whose answer may alter or interpret the definition of done.", "rejection_test": "tests/test_retry.py::test_a_question_is_never_retried_even_when_counsel_verdict_is_answer", "severity": "Harmless when no counsel answer exists; blocking when a question receives an answer and the next pass automatically starts another attempt."}, {"title": "--again bypasses person-only stops, not just exhausted retry budgets", "specimen": "attavo/drive.py::_pass_once calls _advance_again for every stopped state that is neither presently eligible nor waiting. Thus --again can restart claims-boundary, environment, gate, unanswered/person-ruled question, and patch stops, although the approved narrowing permits it only after a stage\u2019s retry budget or early stop is spent.", "retires": "The old broad --again escape hatch inside states reserved for an operator or later breaker behavior.", "rejection_test": "tests/test_retry.py::test_again_refuses_person_patch_claims_boundary_gate_and_environment_stops", "severity": "Harmless without --again; blocking when --again is issued against a person-only or never-retried stop and creates a new marker."}], "tests_named": ["tests/test_retry.py::test_ceiling_recovery_terminates_the_actual_worker_and_it_cannot_write_a_late_record", "tests/test_retry.py::test_a_recovered_retried_attempt_records_retry_of_and_steer", "tests/test_retry.py::test_two_identical_recovered_failures_run_counsel_once_at_exhaustion_and_report_its_sentence", "tests/test_retry.py::test_a_question_is_never_retried_even_when_counsel_verdict_is_answer", "tests/test_retry.py::test_again_refuses_person_patch_claims_boundary_gate_and_environment_stops"]}